IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Housing and Development Act 1959 (Singapore) -- buying, keeping, dealing with and losing a flat sold by the Housing and
-- Development Board: who may not buy (s 50(1)); when an application may be cancelled (s 50(12)); the void sale within the minimum
-- occupation period (s 55); dealings without consent (s 56); the flat's protection from creditors, the Official Assignee and trusts
-- (s 58); the Board's power over a deceased owner's flat (s 59); re-entry (s 62); compulsory acquisition and its timetable
-- (ss 63, 66, 68, 69); the false-information and dangerous-article offences (ss 70, 72); the ceiling on the financial penalty the
-- rules may let the Board impose instead (s 74(1)(i)-(k)); and, for upgrading, the 75% poll, the improvement contribution and its
-- charge on the flat (ss 77(4), (9), 80(1)-(2), 82(1)).
--
-- SEAT: the owner of an HDB flat, or a person applying to buy one from the Board (for s 59 and s 80(2), the personal
-- representative, spouse or beneficiary of an owner who has died). Every decision is phrased as that person would ask it.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 15 July 2026, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/HDA1959.txt (retrieved 1 October 2026).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: Parts 1-3 (the Board, its constitution, functions, powers of entry, offences about its name and symbol, parking,
-- composition), Part 5 and Part 6 (finance and miscellaneous), the Schedules; in Part 4: ss 49, 51, 52-54, 57, 60, 61 (management
-- corporations), 64, 65 (search and examination), 67 (compensation), 71, 73; s 74 beyond its penalty ceilings; Part 4A beyond
-- ss 77(4), (9), 80(1)-(2) and 82(1); Part 4B (design-build-and-sell). The rules made under s 74 (minimum occupation period,
-- eligibility conditions, the financial-penalty rules) are not deposited: where the Act defers to them, the answer is an input.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual to
-- whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test
-- pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Housing and Development Act 1959 -- the flat owner`

§§ `Dates`

-- A period "of N months" is counted by moving the calendar month on N times and keeping the day of the month (an inference: the
-- Act does not say how a month is counted). A day that does not exist in the target month (31 August plus 6 months) rolls into the
-- next month in daydate; no case here turns on it.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`months after` n d MEANS
    Date (DATE_DAY d) (DATE_MONTH d PLUS n) (DATE_YEAR d)

-- What the Act lets the Board do after a notice, read from the seat of the person who got the notice.
DECLARE `When the Board may act` IS ONE OF
    `from` HAS `the earliest day` IS A DATE
    `not while my appeal to the Minister is pending`
    -- The Minister allowed the appeal, or the Act's timetable does not reach the facts: the encoding gives no date.
    `not covered by this encoding`

DECLARE `My appeal` IS ONE OF
    `I did not appeal`
    `my appeal is pending`
    `my appeal was dismissed or withdrawn on` HAS `the day it was disposed of` IS A DATE
    `my appeal was allowed`

-- "until the expiry of a period of N days after the service of the notice": the period expires at the end of day served + N, so
-- the first day the Board may act is served + N + 1 (an inference about counting; the Act states no rule).
GIVEN n      IS A NUMBER
      served IS A DATE
      appeal IS A `My appeal`
GIVETH A `When the Board may act`
`after a notice period of` n `days served on` served `with` appeal MEANS
    CONSIDER appeal
    WHEN `I did not appeal` THEN `from` (served PLUS (n PLUS 1))
    WHEN `my appeal is pending` THEN `not while my appeal to the Minister is pending`
    WHEN `my appeal was dismissed or withdrawn on` disposed THEN `from` (`the later of` (served PLUS (n PLUS 1)) disposed)
    -- The Minister's decision is "final"; the Act does not say what follows an appeal that succeeds.
    WHEN `my appeal was allowed` THEN `not covered by this encoding`

§§ `50(1), (10) -- who may not buy`

-- s 50(1): "A person is not entitled to purchase any flat ... sold subject to the provisions of this Part if the person, his or her
-- spouse or any authorised occupier -- (a) is the owner of any other flat, house, building or land or has an estate or interest
-- therein; or (b) has, at any time within 30 months immediately prior to the date of making an application to the Board to
-- purchase the same, or between the date of the application and the date of completion of the purchase ..., sold any flat, house,
-- building or land of which the person was the owner, or divested himself or herself of any interest therein."
-- s 50(10): the Board "may, in its discretion or on the direction of the Minister, exempt any person".
-- s 2: "authorised occupier" -- a person named in the application as intending to reside, or authorised in writing by the Board
-- to reside (gloss: the people who will live in the flat with me). Whether someone is one is asked as a fact.
-- Other conditions of eligibility (income, citizenship, family nucleus) are for rules under s 74(1)(c), not deposited.
DECLARE `Purchase application` HAS
    `the date I applied to the Board`                                  IS A DATE
    `the date the purchase completed, or today if it has not`          IS A DATE
    `I, my spouse or an authorised occupier owns other property`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dates any of us sold or divested ourselves of property`       IS A LIST OF DATE
    `the Board has exempted me from section 50`                        IS A BOOLEAN

-- The window runs from 30 months before the application to completion; a disposal exactly 30 months before is read as inside it
-- (inference: "within 30 months immediately prior" taken as inclusive).
GIVEN a IS A `Purchase application`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disposal falls in the section 50(1)(b) window` IF
        `months after` 30 d AT LEAST a's `the date I applied to the Board`
    AND d AT MOST a's `the date the purchase completed, or today if it has not`

GIVEN a IS A `Purchase application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred by section 50 from buying a flat from the Board` IF
        NOT a's `the Board has exempted me from section 50`
    AND (   a's `I, my spouse or an authorised occupier owns other property`
         OR any (GIVEN d YIELD `the disposal falls in the section 50(1)(b) window` a d)
                (a's `the dates any of us sold or divested ourselves of property`))

§§ `50(3)-(5) -- if I bought in breach of s 50(1)`

-- s 50(3): on discovery the Board must serve notice of its intention to vest the flat in itself or to terminate the agreement for
-- a lease and re-enter. (3A): it "must not proceed ... until the expiry of a period of 14 days after the service of the notice".
-- (4): "The purchaser may, within 14 days after the service of the notice, appeal to the Minister whose decision is final".
-- (5): if I appeal, the Board must not vest or repossess "until the appeal has been disposed of".
-- (9): the Board may, in its discretion, forfeit moneys paid or deposited.
GIVEN served IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day I can appeal to the Minister against a section 50 notice` served MEANS served PLUS 14

GIVEN served IS A DATE
      appeal IS A `My appeal`
GIVETH A `When the Board may act`
`When can the Board take my flat for a section 50 breach` served appeal MEANS
    `after a notice period of` 14 `days served on` served `with` appeal

§§ `50(12) -- when my application can be cancelled`

-- s 50(12): the Board may cancel an application where -- (a) "the applicant has made any misrepresentation of a material fact or
-- false statement in a material particular, whether innocently or otherwise"; (b) the applicant, spouse or "any person above the
-- age of 14 years listed in his or her application" has been convicted under s 304A, 336, 337 or 338 of the Penal Code 1871 "in
-- connection with the throwing of any matter or thing from any property belonging to, sold by or leased from the Board";
-- (c) a Government CPF cash grant used for the price or loan has not been returned when required; (d) the applicant, spouse or a
-- listed person has been convicted of an immigration offence for giving food or shelter to, or helping to evade apprehension,
-- a person in Singapore in contravention of immigration law. "may" -- the Board's choice; the answer is whether it can.
DECLARE `Application facts` HAS
    `I made a material misrepresentation or false statement, even innocently` IS A BOOLEAN
    `one of us was convicted of a killer-litter offence from Board property`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `I failed to return a CPF cash grant when required`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `one of us was convicted of harbouring an immigration offender`            IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN f IS AN `Application facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Board cancel my application to buy a flat` IF
        f's `I made a material misrepresentation or false statement, even innocently`
    OR  f's `one of us was convicted of a killer-litter offence from Board property`
    OR  f's `I failed to return a CPF cash grant when required`
    OR  f's `one of us was convicted of harbouring an immigration offender`

§§ `55, 56 -- selling and dealing with my flat`

-- s 55(1): "Except with the prior written consent of the Board, an owner ... must not, within the prescribed minimum occupation
-- period, by contract, agreement or otherwise, sell or agree to sell his or her flat". (2): unless the Board authorises otherwise,
-- every sale contract with a purchaser other than the Board "must be in the prescribed form". (3): "Any contract, agreement or
-- other document which is made on or after 20 November 1998 in contravention of subsection (1) or (2) is void."
-- The minimum occupation period is prescribed by rules not deposited: whether it has ended is a fact.
DECLARE `Sale agreement` HAS
    `the date I made the agreement`                               IS A DATE
    `my minimum occupation period had ended by then`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `I had the Board's prior written consent to sell`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement is in the prescribed form`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Board authorised another form`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the buyer is the Board`                                      IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN s IS A `Sale agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my agreement to sell my flat void` IF
        s's `the date I made the agreement` AT LEAST Date 20 11 1998
    AND (   (    NOT s's `my minimum occupation period had ended by then`
             AND NOT s's `I had the Board's prior written consent to sell`)
         OR (    NOT s's `the buyer is the Board`
             AND NOT s's `the agreement is in the prescribed form`
             AND NOT s's `the Board authorised another form`))

-- s 56(1): no flat sold under Part 4 "may be sold, leased, mortgaged or disposed of without the prior written consent of the Board".
-- (2): if such a dealing without consent is registered, "the Board may, by an instrument lodged ... declare [it] to be void".
GIVEN `the dealing is registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `I had the Board's prior written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Board have my sale, lease or mortgage declared void` IF
    `the dealing is registered` AND NOT `I had the Board's prior written consent`

§§ `58 -- my flat and my creditors`

-- s 58(1): "any contract or agreement to directly or indirectly use protected property (or the proceeds of sale ...) as security or
-- collateral for any debt, obligation or claim is void", except (4) security in favour of (a) the Board; (b) an approved financial
-- institution; or (c) a person prescribed by the Minister. (12): "approved financial institution" -- a bank or merchant bank
-- licensed under the Banking Act 1970, a finance company licensed under the Finance Companies Act 1967, a direct insurer licensed
-- under the Insurance Act 1966. "protected property" -- any flat, house or other building sold by the Board under Part 4.
DECLARE `Secured creditor` IS ONE OF
    `the Board`
    `a licensed bank`
    `a licensed merchant bank`
    `a licensed finance company`
    `a licensed direct insurer`
    `a person prescribed by the Minister`
    `a licensed moneylender or any other lender`

GIVEN lender IS A `Secured creditor`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my agreement to use my flat as security void` IF
    CONSIDER lender
    WHEN `a licensed moneylender or any other lender` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 58(6): "No protected property is to vest in the Official Assignee on the bankruptcy of the owner thereof."
-- (8): (6) and (7) do not apply "if the sole owner ... is not a citizen of Singapore or, where there is more than one owner, all the
-- owners are not citizens of Singapore".
GIVEN `no owner of the flat is a Singapore citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my flat vest in the Official Assignee if I am made bankrupt` IF
    `no owner of the flat is a Singapore citizen`

-- s 58(7): "No protected property is to be attached in execution of an order of any court unless the order ... is obtained by --
-- (a) a mortgagee ... under a mortgage created with the prior written consent of the Board ...; or (b) a chargee ... under a
-- charge under any written law over that property." Subject to (8).
DECLARE `Judgment creditor` IS ONE OF
    `a mortgagee under a mortgage made with the Board's consent`
    `a chargee under a charge under written law`
    `any other creditor with a court order`

GIVEN creditor IS A `Judgment creditor`
      `no owner of the flat is a Singapore citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my flat be attached to enforce a court order` IF
        `no owner of the flat is a Singapore citizen`
    OR  CONSIDER creditor
        WHEN `any other creditor with a court order` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 58(9): "No trust in respect of any protected property may be created by the owner thereof without the prior written approval of
-- the Board." (10): such a trust "is void". (11): "No person is to become entitled to any protected property (or any interest in such
-- property) under any resulting trust or constructive trust whensoever created or arising."
DECLARE `Trust over my flat` IS ONE OF
    `a trust I created`
    `a resulting trust`
    `a constructive trust`

GIVEN trust IS A `Trust over my flat`, `the Board approved it in writing beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can this trust give anyone an interest in my flat` IF
    CONSIDER trust
    WHEN `a trust I created` THEN `the Board approved it in writing beforehand`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `59 -- when the owner dies`

-- s 59(1): transmission on death, or a transfer by the personal representatives, must not be registered without the Board's written
-- consent; (2) if the Board refuses consent it may have the flat vested in itself. (3): it may also do so where -- (a) "no
-- representation has been taken out ... within 12 months from the death of the owner"; (b) "representation has been taken out but
-- the personal representatives do not apply for the written consent of the Board ... within 6 months from the date of
-- representation"; or (c) they have consent "but the sale or transfer ... is not completed within 12 months from the date of that
-- written consent". (Gloss: "representation" -- a grant of probate or letters of administration.)
-- Read literally, (a) is met when no grant was taken out within the 12 months, even if one was taken out later (a reading; the
-- Act does not say that a late grant cures it). Each limb is met only once its period has run by the day asked about.
-- s 59(4) (rescission of an agreement for a lease) is not encoded.
DECLARE `Deceased owner's flat` HAS
    `the date of death`                                        IS A DATE
    `the date representation was taken out`                    IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date we applied for the Board's consent`              IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date the Board gave consent`                          IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date the sale or transfer completed`                  IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the Board refused consent`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date I am asking about`                               IS A DATE

-- "not done within N months from the start": the period has run by the day asked, and the step was not done on or before its
-- last day.
GIVEN n       IS A NUMBER
      start   IS A DATE
      done    IS A MAYBE DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `not done within` n `months from` start `by` done `as at` `today` IF
        `today` GREATER THAN `months after` n start
    AND CONSIDER done
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST d THEN d GREATER THAN `months after` n start

GIVEN f IS A `Deceased owner's flat`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Board have the deceased owner's flat vested in itself` IF
        f's `the Board refused consent`
    OR  `not done within` 12 `months from` (f's `the date of death`) `by` (f's `the date representation was taken out`)
            `as at` (f's `the date I am asking about`)
    OR  CONSIDER f's `the date representation was taken out`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST r THEN `not done within` 6 `months from` r `by` (f's `the date we applied for the Board's consent`)
                             `as at` (f's `the date I am asking about`)
    OR  CONSIDER f's `the date the Board gave consent`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST c THEN `not done within` 12 `months from` c `by` (f's `the date the sale or transfer completed`)
                             `as at` (f's `the date I am asking about`)

-- s 59(5): the Board must serve written notice of its intention, and of the compensation; (5A) it "must not proceed ... until the
-- expiry of a period of 28 days after the service of the notice"; (6) the personal representatives and anyone interested in the
-- estate "may, within 28 days after the date of the service of the notice, appeal to the Minister"; (7) no vesting until the appeal
-- is disposed of.
GIVEN served IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day to appeal to the Minister against a section 59 notice` served MEANS served PLUS 28

GIVEN served IS A DATE
      appeal IS A `My appeal`
GIVETH A `When the Board may act`
`When can the Board vest the deceased owner's flat` served appeal MEANS
    `after a notice period of` 28 `days served on` served `with` appeal

§§ `62 -- re-entry and the end of my lease`

-- s 62(1): the Board "may re-enter ... and thereupon the lease determines absolutely -- (a) if the rent ... is unpaid for 3 calendar
-- months after becoming payable and the Board has sent a written demand by registered post ...; (b) if the owner has committed any
-- breach of a condition against assigning, underletting or parting with possession ... or ... of any other condition the breach of
-- which is not capable of remedy and the Board has sent a written notice by registered post ...; (c) if any condition (being a
-- condition the breach of which is capable of remedy) ... is not performed or observed within 2 weeks after a written notice has
-- been sent ...; (d) if the owner has submitted a false statement in the owner's application form ...; (e) if the owner has, in
-- the opinion of the Board, committed a breach of any of the rules made under section 74(1)(g); or (f) if the owner has, without
-- the prior written approval of the Board, used or allowed the use of the flat ... otherwise than for the purpose permitted by the
-- lease." "lease" includes an agreement for a lease (s 2). Limb (e) turns on the Board's opinion: it is an input.
DECLARE `Re-entry facts` HAS
    `the date the unpaid rent became payable`                         IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the Board sent a written demand for the rent by registered post` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I breached the condition against assigning, subletting or parting with possession, or another irremediable condition` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Board sent written notice of that breach by registered post` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date the Board sent notice of a remediable breach`           IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date I remedied it`                                          IS A MAYBE DATE
    `I made a false statement in my application form`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Board is of the opinion that I breached the rules under s 74(1)(g)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I used the flat for an unpermitted purpose without approval`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date I am asking about`                                      IS A DATE

-- (a): "unpaid for 3 calendar months after becoming payable" -- read as still unpaid on the day 3 months after it fell due.
-- (c): "within 2 weeks after a written notice has been sent" -- the 14 days after the day of sending.
GIVEN r IS A `Re-entry facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Board re-enter my flat and end my lease` IF
        (    r's `the Board sent a written demand for the rent by registered post`
         AND CONSIDER r's `the date the unpaid rent became payable`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
             WHEN JUST due THEN r's `the date I am asking about` AT LEAST `months after` 3 due)
    OR  (    r's `I breached the condition against assigning, subletting or parting with possession, or another irremediable condition`
         AND r's `the Board sent written notice of that breach by registered post`)
    OR  CONSIDER r's `the date the Board sent notice of a remediable breach`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST sent THEN
                r's `the date I am asking about` GREATER THAN sent PLUS 14
            AND CONSIDER r's `the date I remedied it`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
                WHEN JUST fixed THEN fixed GREATER THAN sent PLUS 14
    OR  r's `I made a false statement in my application form`
    OR  r's `the Board is of the opinion that I breached the rules under s 74(1)(g)`
    OR  r's `I used the flat for an unpermitted purpose without approval`

§§ `63 -- compulsory acquisition`

-- s 63(1): the Board may compulsorily acquire a flat sold under Part 4 -- (a) "if the owner thereof and his or her spouse (if any)
-- has, in the opinion of the Board, ceased to occupy the same"; (b) if the owner, spouse or any authorised occupier "has at any time
-- ... acquired ... any title to or an estate or interest in any other flat, house or building or land"; (c) unpermitted use without
-- approval; (d) "permitted any person other than an authorised occupier to reside or stay"; (e) failed to perform a lease condition
-- after written notice; (f) misleading or false statement in the application; (g) misrepresentation of a material fact, "whether
-- innocently or otherwise"; (ga) the same as to an acquisition from, or transfer to, a related person; (h) assigns, underlets or
-- parts with possession without consent; (i) "in the opinion of the Board" not occupied by the minimum number or by such persons as
-- the Board requires; (j) "ceased to be a citizen of Singapore" or "ceased to be a permanent resident"; (k) rent or other payment
-- unpaid 3 calendar months after due and a notice of demand sent; (l) CPF cash grant not returned; (m) killer-litter conviction on or
-- after 1 March 1984 of the owner, spouse or an authorised occupier above 14; (n) harbouring conviction; (o) the owner or an
-- authorised occupier who is a related person or above 18 convicted, on or after the appointed date, of an abatement or exclusion
-- offence (Community Disputes Resolution Act 2015) with at least one other such offence convicted, taken into consideration or
-- compounded.
-- (2): (b) "does not apply to any owner ... who has purchased or acquired, with the prior written consent of the Board, any
-- commercial property not exceeding in value $250,000 or such higher value as the Minister may allow, and that commercial property is
-- used or intended to be used ... for business purposes". (10): the Minister may direct the Board to exempt any person.
-- The "appointed date" in (o) is the commencement of s 36 of the Community Disputes Resolution (Amendment) Act 2024, not stated in the
-- deposit: whether the conviction fell on or after it is a fact. Limb (k)'s 3-month count is collapsed into one fact.
DECLARE `Acquisition facts` HAS
    `the Board is of the opinion that I and my spouse have ceased to occupy the flat` IS A BOOLEAN
    `one of us acquired an interest in other property`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was commercial property bought with the Board's prior written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `its value`                                                            IS A NUMBER
    `the higher value the Minister allows`                                 IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `it is used or meant for business`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `I used the flat for an unpermitted purpose without approval`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `I let someone other than an authorised occupier live or stay`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `I failed to perform a lease condition after written notice`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `I made a misleading or false statement or a material misrepresentation in buying` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I sublet or parted with possession without consent`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Board is of the opinion that the flat is not occupied as it requires` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I ceased to be a citizen or a permanent resident`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `a payment to the Board has been unpaid 3 months after a notice of demand` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I failed to return a CPF cash grant when required`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `one of us was convicted of a killer-litter offence on or after 1 March 1984` IS A BOOLEAN
    `one of us was convicted of harbouring an immigration offender`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `a repeat abatement or exclusion offence on or after the appointed date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has directed that I be exempted`                         IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN a IS AN `Acquisition facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the commercial property ceiling for` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a's `the higher value the Minister allows`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 250000
    WHEN JUST v THEN v

GIVEN a IS AN `Acquisition facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 63(2) commercial property exception applies` IF
        a's `it was commercial property bought with the Board's prior written consent`
    AND a's `its value` AT MOST `the commercial property ceiling for` a
    AND a's `it is used or meant for business`

-- (f), (g) and (ga) are taken together as one fact.
GIVEN a IS AN `Acquisition facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Board compulsorily acquire my flat` IF
        NOT a's `the Minister has directed that I be exempted`
    AND (   a's `the Board is of the opinion that I and my spouse have ceased to occupy the flat`
         OR (a's `one of us acquired an interest in other property` AND NOT `the section 63(2) commercial property exception applies` a)
         OR a's `I used the flat for an unpermitted purpose without approval`
         OR a's `I let someone other than an authorised occupier live or stay`
         OR a's `I failed to perform a lease condition after written notice`
         OR a's `I made a misleading or false statement or a material misrepresentation in buying`
         OR a's `I sublet or parted with possession without consent`
         OR a's `the Board is of the opinion that the flat is not occupied as it requires`
         OR a's `I ceased to be a citizen or a permanent resident`
         OR a's `a payment to the Board has been unpaid 3 months after a notice of demand`
         OR a's `I failed to return a CPF cash grant when required`
         OR a's `one of us was convicted of a killer-litter offence on or after 1 March 1984`
         OR a's `one of us was convicted of harbouring an immigration offender`
         OR a's `a repeat abatement or exclusion offence on or after the appointed date`)

§§ `63(5), (7), 66, 68, 69 -- the acquisition timetable`

-- s 63(5): an owner who objects "may, within 28 days after the service of a notice mentioned in subsection (3), submit in writing ...
-- precisely the grounds"; (7) an appeal against the Board's decision on the objection "must be made to the Minister within 28 days
-- after the date of service of the decision".
GIVEN served IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day I can object to the acquisition` served MEANS served PLUS 28

GIVEN `decision served` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day I can appeal to the Minister against the decision on my objection` `decision served` MEANS
    `decision served` PLUS 28

-- s 66(1)(a): the Board may lodge the instrument of vesting "(i) in the case where no objection has been made pursuant to
-- section 63(5) -- on the expiry of a period of 28 days after the date of service of the notice ...; and (ii) in the case where an
-- appeal has been made to the Minister -- at any time after the appeal has been determined by the Minister or when the appeal is
-- withdrawn". The Act gives no time for an owner who objected and did not appeal: that case is not covered.
GIVEN served       IS A DATE
      `I objected` IS A BOOLEAN
      appeal       IS A `My appeal`
GIVETH A `When the Board may act`
`When can the Board vest my acquired flat in itself` served `I objected` appeal MEANS
    IF NOT `I objected`
    THEN `from` (served PLUS 29)
    ELSE CONSIDER appeal
         WHEN `I did not appeal` THEN `not covered by this encoding`
         WHEN `my appeal is pending` THEN `not while my appeal to the Minister is pending`
         WHEN `my appeal was dismissed or withdrawn on` disposed THEN `from` (disposed PLUS 1)
         WHEN `my appeal was allowed` THEN `not covered by this encoding`

-- s 68(1): once the flat is vested in the Board under s 50, 59 or 66, "the Board may proceed to take possession ... on the expiry
-- of a period of 30 days after the service of a notice on the owner".
GIVEN served IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the earliest day the Board can take possession of my flat` served MEANS served PLUS 31

-- s 69(1)-(2): the Board may require me to take delivery of my things within a period that "must be at least 30 days after the date
-- of service of the notice"; (4) after that it may dispose of them; (6) proceeds go first to storage and disposal costs and debts
-- owed to the Board, the balance to me.
GIVEN served IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the earliest day the Board can make my deadline to collect my belongings` served MEANS served PLUS 30

§§ `70, 72 -- offences`

DECLARE `Maximum punishment` HAS
    `fine`                      IS A NUMBER
    `months of imprisonment`    IS A NUMBER
    `both may be imposed`       IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 70: any person who, "in relation to the purchase, mortgage, sale or transfer ... of a flat" or "in relation to any application
-- ... to the Board for its permission, consent, approval or licence", "makes ... any statement to the Board which is false, and which
-- the person either knows or believes to be false or does not believe to be true, shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both".
GIVEN `the statement was about buying, mortgaging, selling or transferring a flat, or an application to the Board` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement was false`                                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
      `I knew or believed it false, or did not believe it true`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed the offence of giving the Board false information` IF
        `the statement was about buying, mortgaging, selling or transferring a flat, or an application to the Board`
    AND `the statement was false`
    AND `I knew or believed it false, or did not believe it true`

`What is the most I can be given for giving the Board false information` MEANS
    `Maximum punishment` WITH
        `fine`                   IS 5000
        `months of imprisonment` IS 6
        `both may be imposed`    IS TRUE

-- s 72(1): the Board may by written notice direct an owner, lessee or occupier to remove "any article or object placed by any window
-- or on any balcony ... in a manner which is likely to cause any damage to property or injury to life". (2): failing to comply -- "a
-- fine not exceeding $2,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine of $100 for every day during which the offence
-- continues after conviction". No imprisonment.
GIVEN `days the failure continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be fined for not removing a dangerous article` `days the failure continued after conviction` MEANS
    2000 PLUS 100 TIMES `days the failure continued after conviction`

§§ `74(1)(i)-(k) -- a financial penalty instead`

-- s 74(1): the Minister may make rules on (i) the Board's power to impose "a financial penalty not exceeding $50,000" on an owner or
-- applicant for a breach of s 50 "on or after 20 July 2015 where the Board does not proceed against that owner or applicant under
-- section 50"; (j) the same for s 62; (k) "instead of acquiring" under s 63(1), the same for s 63. The rules are not deposited: this
-- gives the Act's ceiling, not the amount, and nothing at all for a breach before 20 July 2015.
GIVEN `the date of the breach` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most financial penalty the Board can impose on me instead of acting under section 50, 62 or 63` `the date of the breach` MEANS
    IF `the date of the breach` AT LEAST Date 20 7 2015
    THEN JUST 50000
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `77, 80, 82 -- upgrading my block`

-- s 77(4): the Board may, "with the Minister's approval", carry out general upgrading works "if it appears from a poll ... that 75%
-- or more of the total value in votes of all prescribed owners of all flats within the precinct have been cast in favour". (9): flat
-- upgrading works likewise, 75% of the value in votes of the owners of flats "within each such building". (Gloss: "value in votes" --
-- votes weighted as the rules prescribe; the weighting is not deposited, so the values are inputs.)
GIVEN `value of votes in favour` IS A NUMBER
      `total value of votes of all prescribed owners` IS A NUMBER
      `the Minister approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Board carry out the upgrading works on my block` IF
        `the Minister approved`
    AND `total value of votes of all prescribed owners` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `value of votes in favour` TIMES 100 AT LEAST 75 TIMES `total value of votes of all prescribed owners`

-- s 80(1): an owner liable for an improvement contribution "must, upon a written demand by the Board, pay ... not later than one month
-- from the date of the written demand". (3) late payment carries prescribed interest and penalty.
GIVEN `demand date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I pay the improvement contribution` `demand date` MEANS `months after` 1 `demand date`

-- s 82(1): if the contribution "remains unpaid on the expiry of the period of 3 months after the Board has served ... a written
-- demand", it, with interest and penalty, "constitutes a charge on the flat on the expiry of that period in favour of the Board";
-- (2) the Board then has a power of sale.
GIVEN `demand served` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`On what day does my unpaid improvement contribution become a charge on my flat` `demand served` MEANS
    `months after` 3 `demand served` PLUS 1

-- s 80(2): where no representation has been taken out for a deceased owner, or the personal representatives "fail to apply for the
-- written consent of the Board", the Board "may ... require the spouse (if any) of the deceased owner or any beneficiary of the
-- deceased owner's estate who has attained the age of 21 years to pay the improvement contribution as if it is a debt owed by him or
-- her", recoverable from the estate. Read as: the age condition attaches to the beneficiary, not the spouse (a reading).
GIVEN `I am the deceased owner's spouse`                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a beneficiary of the estate`                     IS A BOOLEAN
      `my age`                                               IS A NUMBER
      `no representation has been taken out, or the personal representatives failed to apply for consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Board make me pay the deceased owner's improvement contribution` IF
        `no representation has been taken out, or the personal representatives failed to apply for consent`
    AND (   `I am the deceased owner's spouse`
         OR (`I am a beneficiary of the estate` AND `my age` AT LEAST 21))
